  "notes": [
   "COMM 235 is printed as an option both for the oral communication requirement (with COMM C1000) and for the critical thinking requirement (with ENG 111); it is recorded once, under COMM C1000. Footnote 1: it can satisfy only one core requirement, not both.",
   "List A pairs lectures with labs as single choices (BIOL 140 & BIOL 141, ERTH 101/101H & ERTH 102, ERTH 111/111H & ERTH 111L, ERTH 112 & 112L, ERTH 151 & 151L, PHYS 101 & 101L); labs are recorded as separate entries but are taken with their lecture as one choice. Footnote 2: at least one of the two List A courses must have a lab.",
   "The '3' printed after HIST 107, HIST 108, HIST C1001 and HIST C1002 in Lists B and C is footnote 3, not units: these HIST courses can satisfy only one section (List B or List C), not both. They are listed in both blocks as printed.",
   "ERTH 142/GEOG 105 is printed as one cross-listed course; recorded as ERTH 142 with GEOG 105 as alternative.",
   "List C ends with 'Foreign Language' with no course code; not recorded as a course.",
   "Catalog prints ARTH C1100/C1100H/C1200/C1200H with a space; closed list stores ARTHC1100 etc. Treated as the same courses (catalog_addition false).",
